PROBLEM STATEMENT:
Write a program to count the number of days between two dates.
The two dates are given as strings in the format YYYY-MM-DD.
Return the absolute difference in days between the two dates.
JAVA CODE:
import java.time.LocalDate;
import java.time.temporal.ChronoUnit;

class Solution {
    public int daysBetweenDates(String date1, String date2) {
        // Parse the strings into LocalDate objects
        LocalDate d1 = LocalDate.parse(date1);
        LocalDate d2 = LocalDate.parse(date2);

        // Calculate the difference in days
        long diff = ChronoUnit.DAYS.between(d1, d2);

        // Return absolute value since order doesn't matter
        return (int) Math.abs(diff);
    }
}
INPUT:
date1 = "2020-01-15"
date2 = "2019-12-31"
OUTPUT:
15
